#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:49
msgctxt "id=\"title\""
msgid "22 Years of KDE"
msgstr "Los 22 años de KDE"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:50
msgctxt "id=\"intro\""
msgid ""
"A tour through the moments that marked the 22 years of community history, "
"starting with the technologies that made possible its existence.See our KDE "
"20 years <a style=\"text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://20years.kde."
"org/book/index.html\">book</a>."
msgstr ""
"Un percorríu pente los momentos que marcaron los 22 años de la historia de "
"la comunidá, comenzando peles teunoloxíes que ficieron posible la so "
"esistencia. Mira'l <a style=\"text-decoration:underline;\" href="
"\"https://20years.kde.org/book/index.html\">llibru</a> de los 20 años de KDE."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:52
msgctxt "id=\"start\""
msgid "Start<i class=\"fa fa-chevron-down\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>"
msgstr "Aniciar<i class=\"fa fa-chevron-down\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:58
msgctxt "id=\"all-lbl\""
msgid "All"
msgstr "Toos"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:61
msgctxt "id=\"floss-events-lbl\""
msgid "FLOSS Events"
msgstr "Eventos FLOSS"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:64
msgctxt "id=\"kde-events-lbl\""
msgid "KDE Events"
msgstr "Eventos de KDE"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:67
msgctxt "id=\"meetings-lbl\""
msgid "Meetings"
msgstr "Conceyos"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:70
msgctxt "id=\"releases-lbl\""
msgid "Releases"
msgstr "Versiones"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:84
msgctxt "id=\"box01-title\""
msgid "UNIX is born"
msgstr "Naz UNIX"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:91
msgctxt "id=\"box01\""
msgid ""
"In 1969, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Thompson\">Ken "
"Thompson</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dennis_Ritchie"
"\">Dennis Ritchie</a> started working on <a href=\"http://www.unix.org/"
"what_is_unix/history_timeline.html\">UNIX</a>. Initially written in "
"assembler, it was soon rewritten in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"C_(programming_language)\">C</a>, a language created by Ritchie and "
"considered high level."
msgstr ""
"En 1969, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Thompson\">Ken "
"Thompson</a> y <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dennis_Ritchie"
"\">Dennis Ritchie</a> comenzaron a trabayar n'<a href=\"http://www.unix.org/"
"what_is_unix/history_timeline.html\">UNIX</a>. Escritu nel aniciu "
"n'ensamblador, pronto lu reescribieron en <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/"
"wiki/C_(programming_language)\">C</a>, un llingüaxe creáu por Ritchie y "
"consideráu de nivel altu."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:100
msgctxt "id=\"box02-title\""
msgid "C++ was created"
msgstr "Creóse C++"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:107
msgctxt "id=\"box02\""
msgid ""
"In 1979, <a href=\"http://www.stroustrup.com/bio.html\">Bjarne Stroustrup</"
"a> started developing \"C with classes\", which would later become the <a "
"href=\"http://www.softwarepreservation.org/projects/c_plus_plus/\">C ++</a>. "
"In his opinion, it was the only language of the time that allowed to write "
"programs that were at the same time efficient and elegant."
msgstr ""
"En 1979, <a href=\"http://www.stroustrup.com/bio.html\">Bjarne Stroustrup</"
"a> comenzó'l desendolcu de «C con clases» que dempués diba convertise en <a "
"href=\"http://www.softwarepreservation.org/projects/c_plus_plus/\">C ++</a>. "
"Na so opinión, yera l'únicu llingüaxe d'entós que permitía escribir "
"programes que yeren eficientes y elegantes al empar."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:116
msgctxt "id=\"box03-title\""
msgid "The beginning of Free Software"
msgstr "El comienzu del software llibre"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:123
msgctxt "id=\"box03\""
msgid ""
"In 1984, <a href=\"https://stallman.org/biographies.html#serious\">Richard "
"Stallman</a> started developing <a href=\"https://www.gnu.org/gnu/about-gnu."
"html\">GNU</a> (GNU is Not Unix), a completely free operating system based "
"on Unix, which was proprietary."
msgstr ""
"En 1984, <a href=\"https://stallman.org/biographies.html#serious\">Richard "
"Stallman</a> comenzó'l desendolcu de <a href=\"https://www.gnu.org/gnu/about-"
"gnu.html\">GNU</a> (GNU in Not Unix «GNU nun ye Unix»), un sistema  "
"operativu llibre dafechu basáu en Unix, que yera privativu."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:133
msgctxt "id=\"box04-title\""
msgid "The Linux Kernel"
msgstr "El kernel Linux"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:140
msgctxt "id=\"box04\""
msgid ""
"In 1991, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linus_Torvalds\">Linus "
"Torvalds</a> created the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_kernel"
"\">Linux kernel</a> based on <a href=\"http://www.minix3.org/\">MINIX</a>, a "
"version of Unix written by <a href=\"http://www.cs.vu.nl/~ast/home/faq.html"
"\">Andrew Tanenbaum</a>. The emergence of Linux has revolutionized the "
"history of free software and helped to popularize it. See the <a href="
"\"https://web.archive.org/web/20190628003733im_/https://www.linux.com/sites/"
"lcom/files/styles/rendered_file/public/linux-kernel-development-"
"infographic-2016.jpg?itok=DqVqiplt\">25 Years of Linux Kernel Development "
"infographic</a>."
msgstr ""
"En 1991, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linus_Torvalds\">Linus "
"Torvalds</a> creó'l <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_kernel"
"\">kernel Linux</a> basáu en <a href=\"http://www.minix3.org/\">MINIX</a>, "
"una versión d'Unix escrita por <a href=\"http://www.cs.vu.nl/~ast/home/faq."
"html\">Andrew Tanenbaum</a>. El xurdimientu de Linux revolucionó la historia "
"del software llibre y ayudó a popularizalu. Mira la <a href=\"https://web."
"archive.org/web/20190628003733im_/https://www.linux.com/sites/lcom/files/"
"styles/rendered_file/public/linux-kernel-development-infographic-2016.jpg?"
"itok=DqVqiplt\">infografía de los 25 años de desendolcu del kernel Linux</a>."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:150
msgctxt "id=\"box05-title\""
msgid "The first distros are born"
msgstr "Nacen les primeres distros"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:157
msgctxt "id=\"box05\""
msgid ""
"In 1993, the first free distributions begin to emerge, based in <a href="
"\"http://www.aboutlinux.info/2005/11/complete-concise-history-of-gnulinux."
"html\">GNU and Linux</a>. A <a href=\"http://futurist.se/gldt/\">GNU/Linux "
"distribution</a> is usually formed by the Linux kernel, GNU tools and "
"libraries, and more a collection of applications."
msgstr ""
"En 1993 xurdieron les primeres distribuciones llibres basaes en <a href="
"\"http://www.aboutlinux.info/2005/11/complete-concise-history-of-gnulinux."
"html\">GNU y Linux</a>. Una <a href=\"http://futurist.se/gldt/"
"\">distribución GNU/Linux</a> componse del kernel Linux, les ferramientes y "
"biblioteques de GNU, y más aplicaciones."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:166
msgctxt "id=\"box06-title\""
msgid "Qt was created"
msgstr "Creóse Qt"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:173
msgctxt "id=\"box06\""
msgid ""
"In 1995, the Norwegian company Troll Tech created the cross-platform "
"framework <a href=\"https://wiki.qt.io/About_Qt\">Qt</a>, with which KDE "
"would be created in the following year. Qt became the basis of the main KDE "
"technologies in these 20 years. Learn more about <a href=\"https://wiki.qt."
"io/Qt_History\">Qt History</a>."
msgstr ""
"En 1995, la compaña noruega Troll Tech creó'l framework multiplataforma <a "
"href=\"https://wiki.qt.io/About_Qt\">Qt</a>, col que se crearía KDE al añu "
"siguiente. Qt convirtióse na base fundamental de les teunoloxíes de KDE "
"nestos 20 años. Deprendi más tocante a la <a href=\"https://wiki.qt.io/"
"Qt_History\">historia de Qt</a>."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:182
msgctxt "id=\"box07-title\""
msgid "KDE was announced"
msgstr "Anuncióse KDE"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:189
msgctxt "id=\"box07\""
msgid ""
"In 1996, <a href=\"http://www.linuxjournal.com/article/6834\">Matthias "
"Ettrich</a> announced the creation of Kool Desktop Environment (KDE), a "
"graphical interface for Unix systems, built with Qt and C ++ and designed "
"for the end user. The name \"KDE\" was a pun on the graphic environment <a "
"href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Desktop_Environment\">CDE</a>, "
"which was proprietary at the time. Read <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/"
"announcements/announcement.php\">the original announcement</a> of the KDE "
"Project."
msgstr ""
"En 1996, <a href=\"http://www.linuxjournal.com/article/6834\">Matthias "
"Ettrich</a> anunció la creación del Kool Desktop Environment (KDE), una "
"interfaz gráfica d'usuariu pa sistemes Unix, fecha con Qt y C ++, y diseñada "
"pal usuariu final. El nome «KDE» yera un xuegu de pallabres del entornu "
"gráficu <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Desktop_Environment"
"\">CDE</a>, que yera privativu daquella. Llei <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/"
"announcements/announcement.php\">l'anunciu orixinal</a> del proyeutu KDE."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:198
msgctxt "id=\"box08-title\""
msgid "KDE One Conference"
msgstr "Conferencia KDE One"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:203
msgctxt "id=\"box08\""
msgid ""
"In 1997, about 15 KDE developers met in Arnsberg, Germany, to work on the "
"project and discuss its future. This event became known as <a href=\"https://"
"community.kde.org/KDE_Project_History/KDE_One_(Developer_Meeting)\">KDE One</"
"a>."
msgstr ""
"En 1997, alredor de 15 desendolcadores de KDE aconceyaron n'Arnsberg "
"(Alemaña) pa trabayar nel proyeutu y aldericar el so futuru. Esti eventu "
"conocióse como <a href=\"https://community.kde.org/KDE_Project_History/"
"KDE_One_(Developer_Meeting)\">KDE One</a>."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:210
msgctxt "id=\"box09-title\""
msgid "KDE Beta 1"
msgstr "KDE Beta 1"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:217
msgctxt "id=\"box09\""
msgid ""
"The beta 1 version of KDE was <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/"
"beta1announce.php\">released</a> exactly 12 months after the project "
"announcement. The release text emphasized that KDE was not a window manager, "
"but an integrated environment in which the window manager was just another "
"part."
msgstr ""
"La versión beta 1de KDE <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/"
"beta1announce.php\">llanzóse</a> puramente 12 meses dempués del anunciu del "
"proyeutu. El testu del llanzamientu enfatizaba que KDE nun yera un xestor de "
"ventanes, sinón un entornu integráu nel que'l xestor de ventanes yera namás "
"otru componente."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:223
msgctxt "id=\"box10-title\""
msgid "KDE e.V was founded"
msgstr "Fundóse KDE e.V"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:230
msgctxt "id=\"box10\""
msgid ""
"In 1997, <a href=\"https://ev.kde.org/index.php\">KDE e.V.</a>, the "
"nonprofit that represents the KDE community financially and legally, was "
"founded in Tübingen, Germany."
msgstr ""
"En 1997, <a href=\"https://ev.kde.org/index.php\">KDE e.V.</a>, la "
"organización ensin ánimu de llucru que representa a la comunidá KDE "
"económica y llegalmente, fundóse en Tübingen (Alemaña)."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:240
msgctxt "id=\"box11-title\""
msgid "KDE Free Qt Foundation was created"
msgstr "Creóse la KDE Free Qt Foundation"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:247
msgctxt "id=\"box11\""
msgid ""
"The foundation agreement  for the <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/community/"
"whatiskde/kdefreeqtfoundation.php\">KDE Free Qt Foundation</a> is signed by "
"KDE e.V. and Trolltech, then owner of Qt. The Foundation <a href=\"https://"
"dot.kde.org/2016/01/13/qt-guaranteed-stay-free-and-open-%E2%80%93-legal-"
"update\">ensures the permanent availability</a> of Qt as Free Software."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:253
msgctxt "id=\"box12-title\""
msgid "KDE 1 was released"
msgstr "Llanzóse KDE 1"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:260
msgctxt "id=\"box12\""
msgid ""
"KDE released the <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/announce-1.0.php"
"\">first stable version</a> of its graphical environment in 1998, with "
"highlights as an application development framework,the KOM/OpenParts, and a "
"preview of its office suite. See the <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/"
"screenshots/kde1shots.php\">KDE 1.x Screenshots</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:269
msgctxt "id=\"box13-title\""
msgid "Konqi"
msgstr "Konqi"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:276
msgctxt "id=\"box13\""
msgid ""
"In April 1999, a dragon is announced as the new animated assistant to the "
"KDE Help Center. It was so charming that it replaced the previous project "
"mascot, Kandalf, from version 3.x on. See the <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/"
"screenshots/images/large/kde2b3_5.png\">KDE 2 Screenshot</a> showing Konqi "
"and Kandalf."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:282
msgctxt "id=\"box14-title\""
msgid "KDE Two Conference"
msgstr "Conferencia KDE Two"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:287
msgctxt "id=\"box14\""
msgid ""
"In October 1999, the second meeting of KDE developers took place in "
"Erlangen, Germany. Read the <a href=\"https://community.kde.org/"
"KDE_Project_History/KDE_Two_(Developer_Meeting)\">report</a> on the KDE Two "
"Conference."
msgstr ""
"N'ochobre de 1999, el segundu conceyu de desendolcadores de KDE celebróse "
"n'Erlangen (Alemaña). Llei <a href=\"https://community.kde.org/"
"KDE_Project_History/KDE_Two_(Developer_Meeting)\">l'informe</a> tocante a la "
"conferencia KDE Two."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:296
msgctxt "id=\"box15-title\""
msgid "\"KDE Desktop\""
msgstr "«L'escritoriu KDE»"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:303
msgctxt "id=\"box15\""
msgid ""
"From the <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/announce-1.90.php"
"\">beta 1 version of KDE 2</a> it is possible to perceive a project naming "
"change. The releases that once referred to the project as \"K Desktop "
"Environment\", began referring to it only as \"KDE Desktop\"."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:309
msgctxt "id=\"box16-title\""
msgid "KDE Three Beta Conference"
msgstr "Conferencia KDE Three Beta"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:314
msgctxt "id=\"box16\""
msgid ""
"In July 2000, the third meeting (beta) of KDE developers occurred in Trysil, "
"Norway. <a href=\"https://community.kde.org/KDE_Project_History/"
"KDE_Three_Beta_(Developer_Meeting)\">Find out</a> what was done during the "
"conference."
msgstr ""
"N'ochobre de 1999, el segundu conceyu de desendolcadores de KDE celebróse "
"n'Erlangen (Alemaña). Llei <a href=\"https://community.kde.org/"
"KDE_Project_History/KDE_Two_(Developer_Meeting)\">l'informe</a> tocante a la "
"conferencia KDE Two."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:320
msgctxt "id=\"box17-title\""
msgid "KDE 2 was released"
msgstr "Llanzóse KDE 2"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:327
msgctxt "id=\"box17\""
msgid ""
"KDE <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/announce-2.0.php\">released</"
"a> its second version, featuring as main news <a href=\"https://konqueror."
"org/\">Konqueror</a> web browser and file manager; and the office suite <a "
"href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KOffice\">KOffice</a>. KDE had its code "
"almost entirely  rewritten for this second version. See the <a href="
"\"https://www.kde.org/screenshots/kde2shots.php\">KDE 2.0 Screenshots</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:336
msgctxt "id=\"box18-title\""
msgid "\"KDE Project\""
msgstr "«El proyeutu de KDE»"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:343
msgctxt "id=\"box18\""
msgid ""
"From the <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/announce-2.1.2.php"
"\">release announcement</a> of version 2.1.2 there is also a change of the "
"nomenclature. The announcements began referring to KDE as \"KDE Project\"."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:350
msgctxt "id=\"box19-title\""
msgid "KDE Women"
msgstr "KDE Women"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:357
msgctxt "id=\"box19\""
msgid ""
"In March 2001, the creation of community women's group was announced. The <a "
"href=\"https://community.kde.org/KDE_Women\">KDE Women</a> aimed to help "
"increase the number of women in free software communities, particularly in "
"KDE. Watch to the video <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HTwQ-oGTmGA"
"\">\"Highlights of KDE Women\"</a> of the Akademy 2010."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:366
msgctxt "id=\"box20-title\""
msgid "KDE Three Meeting"
msgstr "Conceyu KDE Three"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:373
msgctxt "id=\"box20\""
msgid ""
"In March 2002, about 25 developers gathered for the <a href=\"https://"
"community.kde.org/KDE_Project_History/KDE_Three_(Developer_Meeting)\">third "
"KDE meeting</a> in Nuremberg, Germany. The KDE 3 was about to be released "
"and the KDE 2 code needed to be migrated to the new library Qt 3."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:379
msgctxt "id=\"box21-title\""
msgid "KDE 3"
msgstr "KDE 3"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:386
msgctxt "id=\"box21\""
msgid ""
"KDE released its <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/announce-3.0.php"
"\">third version</a>, showing as important additions a new print framework, "
"KDEPrint; the translation of the project for 50 languages; and a package of "
"educational applications, maintained by the KDE Edutainment Project. See the "
"<a href=\"https://www.kde.org/screenshots/kde300shots.php\">KDE 3.0 "
"Screenshots</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:392
msgctxt "id=\"box22-title\""
msgid "KDE e.V. meeting"
msgstr "Conceyu de KDE e.V."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:397
msgctxt "id=\"box22\""
msgid ""
"In August 2002, there was a <a href=\"https://ev.kde.org/reports/2002.php"
"\">meeting of board members of the KDE e.V.</a> that was essential to "
"establish how the organization works. At this meeting it was decided, among "
"other things, that the brand \"KDE\" would be registered and that new "
"members should be invited and supported by two active members of e.V."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:406
msgctxt "id=\"box23-title\""
msgid "KDE 3.1"
msgstr "KDE 3.1"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:413
msgctxt "id=\"box23\""
msgid ""
"In <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/announce-3.1.php\">version "
"3.1</a> the community presented KDE with a new look, a new theme for "
"widgets, called Keramik, and Crystal as default theme for the icons. See <a "
"href=\"https://www.kde.org/info/3.1/feature_guide_1.html\">KDE 3.1 New "
"Feature Guide</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:419
msgctxt "id=\"box24-title\""
msgid "Kastle"
msgstr "Kastle"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:426
msgctxt "id=\"box24\""
msgid ""
"In August 2003, about 100 contributors of KDE from various countries "
"gathered in a castle in the Czech Republic. The event was called <a href="
"\"https://akademy.kde.org/2003\">Kastle</a> and was the forerunner of "
"Akademy, the event that would become the international annual meeting of the "
"community."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:435
msgctxt "id=\"box25-title\""
msgid "Akademy 2004"
msgstr "Akademy 2004"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:442
msgctxt "id=\"box25\""
msgid ""
"In August 2004, the <a href=\"https://conference2004.kde.org/\">first "
"international meeting of the community</a> took place. The event was held in "
"Ludwigsburg, Germany, and launched a series of international events called "
"<a href=\"https://akademy.kde.org/\">\"Akademy\"</a> which take place "
"annually since then. The event got its name because it happened in the "
"\"Filmakademie\" city film school. See the <a href=\"http://byte.kde.org/"
"~duffus/akademy/\">group photos</a> of all Akademies."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:451
msgctxt "id=\"box26-title\""
msgid "KDE 3.5"
msgstr "KDE 3.5"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:458
msgctxt "id=\"box26\""
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/announce-3.5.php\">KDE 3.5 was "
"released</a>. This version introduced several new features, among them, the "
"SuperKaramba, a tool that allowed customize your desktop with \"applets\"; "
"the Amarok and Kaffeine players; and the media burner K3B. See <a href="
"\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/visualguide-3.5.php\">KDE 3.5: A Visual "
"Guide to New Features</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:467
msgctxt "id=\"box27-title\""
msgid "First Akademy-Es"
msgstr "Primer Akademy-Es"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:474
msgctxt "id=\"box27\""
msgid ""
"In March 2006, the <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2006/02/10/akademy-es-2006-"
"barcelona\">first meeting</a> of Spanish KDE contributors took place in "
"Barcelona. Since then, Akademy-Es has turned into an annual event. Learn "
"more about <a href=\"https://www.kde-espana.org/\">Spanish KDE contributors "
"group</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:480
msgctxt "id=\"box28-title\""
msgid "KDE Four Core meeting"
msgstr "Conceyu de KDE e.V."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:485
msgctxt "id=\"box28\""
msgid ""
"In July 2006, the developers of the KDE core libraries gathered in Trysill, "
"Norway, for the <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2006/06/26/kde-libs-hackers-"
"meet-kde-four-core\">KDE Four Core meeting</a>. The event was a kind of "
"successor to the KDE Beta Three Conference and KDE Three Meeting and in it "
"developers worked on the development of KDE 4 and stabilization of some core "
"libraries to the project."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:494
msgctxt "id=\"box29-title\""
msgid "Guademy"
msgstr "Guademy"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:501
msgctxt "id=\"box29\""
msgid ""
"In March 2007, several contributors of KDE and <a href=\"https://www.gnome."
"org/\">Gnome</a> met in A Coruña, Spain, an event which sought to establish "
"a collaboration between the two projects. The event became known as <a href="
"\"https://dot.kde.org/2007/03/28/guademy-2007-event-report\">Guademy</a>, a "
"mixture of <a href=\"https://wiki.gnome.org/GUADEC\">Guadec</a>, the name "
"given to the Gnome event with Akademy, KDE event name."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:507
msgctxt "id=\"box30-title\""
msgid "KDE 4 Alpha 1"
msgstr "KDE 4 Alpha 1"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:514
msgctxt "id=\"box30\""
msgid ""
"In May 2007, <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/announce-4.0-alpha1."
"php\">the alpha 1 version of KDE 4</a>, codenamed \"Knut\", was announced. "
"This announcement showed a completely new desktop, with a new theme, Oxygen, "
"new applications like Okular and Dolphin, and a new desktop shell, Plasma. "
"See <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/visualguide-4.0-alpha1.php"
"\">KDE 4.0 Alpha 1: A Visual Guide to New Features</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:520
msgctxt "id=\"box31-title\""
msgid "KDE 4 Development Platform"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:527
msgctxt "id=\"box31\""
msgid ""
"In October 2007, KDE announced the <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/"
"announcements/announce-4.0-platform-rc1.php\">release candidate</a> of its "
"development platform consisting of basic libraries and tools to develop KDE "
"applications."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:536
msgctxt "id=\"box32-title\""
msgid "KDE 4"
msgstr "KDE 4"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:543
msgctxt "id=\"box32\""
msgid ""
"In 2008, the community <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/4.0/"
"\">announced the revolutionary KDE 4</a>. In addition to the visual impact "
"of the new default theme, Oxygen, and the new desktop interface, Plasma; KDE "
"4 also innovated by presenting the following applications: the PDF reader "
"Okular, the Dolphin file manager, as well as KWin, supporting graphics "
"effects. See <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/4.0/guide.php\">KDE "
"4.0 Visual Guide</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:549
msgctxt "id=\"box33-title\""
msgid "\"KDE Community\""
msgstr "«La comunidá de KDE»"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:556
msgctxt "id=\"box33\""
msgid ""
"From the <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/4.1/\">announcement of "
"version 4.1</a> on there was already a tendency to refer to KDE as a "
"\"community\" and not just as a \"project\". This change was recognized and "
"affirmed in the rebranding announcement of the following year."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:565
msgctxt "id=\"box34-title\""
msgid "First Camp KDE"
msgstr "Primer Akademy-Es"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:572
msgctxt "id=\"box34\""
msgid ""
"In January 2009, <a href=\"https://techbase.kde.org/Events/"
"CampKDE/2009\">the first edition of Camp KDE</a> took place in Negril, "
"Jamaica. It was the first KDE event in the Americas. After that, there were "
"two more US-based conferences, <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2010/01/17/day-"
"one-camp-kde-2010\">in 2010 in San Diego</a>, and another <a href=\"https://"
"dot.kde.org/2011/04/13/re-live-camp-kde-experience\">in 2011 in San "
"Francisco</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:579
msgctxt "id=\"box35-title\""
msgid "Gran Canaria Desktop Summit"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:586
msgctxt "id=\"box35\""
msgid ""
"In July 2009, the first <a href=\"http://www.grancanariadesktopsummit.org/"
"\">Desktop Summit</a>, a joint conference of the KDE and Gnome communities, "
"took place in Gran Canaria, Spain. The <a href=\"https://dot.kde."
"org/2009/07/14/vibrant-community-propels-kde-forward-akademy-2009\">Akademy "
"2009</a> was held with this event."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:592
msgctxt "id=\"box36-title\""
msgid "1 million of commits"
msgstr "1 millón d'unvios"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:599
msgctxt "id=\"box36\""
msgid ""
"The community <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2009/07/20/kde-reaches-1000000-"
"commits-its-subversion-repository\">reached the mark of 1 million of "
"commits</a>. From 500,000 in January 2006 and 750,000 in December 2007, only "
"19 months later, contributions reached the 1 million mark. The increase in "
"these contributions coincides with the launch of innovative KDE 4."
msgstr ""
"La comunidá <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2009/07/20/kde-reaches-1000000-"
"commits-its-subversion-repository\">algamó al cifra de 1 millón d'unvios</a>. "
"Dende 500.000 en xineru de 2006 y 750.000 n'avientu de 2007, namás "
"19 meses dempués, los collaboradores algamaron la cifra del millón. L'aumentu "
"nestes collaboraciones coincide col llanzamientu de KDE 4."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:605
msgctxt "id=\"box37-title\""
msgid "First Randa Meetings"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:612
msgctxt "id=\"box37\""
msgid ""
"In September 2009, <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2009/09/08/third-plasma-"
"summit-lifts-kde-desktop-higher-grounds\">the first</a> of a series of "
"events known as <a href=\"https://community.kde.org/Sprints/Randa\">Randa "
"Meetings</a> took place in Randa, in Swiss Alps. The event brought together "
"several sprints of various community projects. Since then, Randa Meetings "
"take place annually."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:618
msgctxt "id=\"box38-title\""
msgid "Rebranding"
msgstr "Anovamientu de la marca"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:625
msgctxt "id=\"box38\""
msgid ""
"In November 2009, the community <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2009/11/24/"
"repositioning-kde-brand\">announced</a> changes to its brand. The name \"K "
"Desktop Environment\" had become ambiguous and obsolete and is replaced by "
"\"KDE\". The name \"KDE\" is no longer just referring to a desktop "
"environment, but now represents both the community and the project umbrella "
"supported by this community."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:631
msgctxt "id=\"box39-title\""
msgid "KDE Software Compilation"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:638
msgctxt "id=\"box39\""
msgid ""
"From <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/announce-4.3.4.php"
"\">version 4.3.4</a> on, KDE announcements began to refer to the whole suite "
"of products as 'KDE Software Compilation' (KDE SC). Currently, this trend is "
"abandoned."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:647
msgctxt "id=\"box40-title\""
msgid "Akademy-Br"
msgstr "Akademy-Br"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:654
msgctxt "id=\"box40\""
msgid ""
"In April 2010, <a href=\"https://wiki.br.kde.org/Akademy-BR_2010\">the first "
"meeting</a> of Brazil KDE contributors took place. The event was held in "
"Salvador, Bahia, and was the only Brazilian Akademy edition. From 2012 on, "
"the event expanded to a meeting for all Latin American contributors."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:660
msgctxt "id=\"box41-title\""
msgid "Join the Game"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:667
msgctxt "id=\"box41\""
msgid ""
"In June 2010, the KDE e.V announced the supporting membership program <a "
"href=\"https://jointhegame.kde.org/\">\"Join the Game\"</a>, which aims to "
"encourage financial support to the community. By participating in the "
"program you become a member of the KDE e.V, contributing to an annual amount "
"and being able participate in the organization's annual meetings."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:673
msgctxt "id=\"box42-title\""
msgid "KDE SC 4.5"
msgstr "KDE SC 4.5"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:680
msgctxt "id=\"box42\""
msgid ""
"In August 2010, the community <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/"
"announcements/4.5/\">announced version 4.5</a> of its products: Development "
"Platform, Applications and Plasma Workspaces. Each of them began to have a "
"separate release announcement. One of the highlights of this version was the "
"Plasma interface for netbooks, announced in version 4.4."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:686
msgctxt "id=\"box43-title\""
msgid "Calligra Suite"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:693
msgctxt "id=\"box43\""
msgid ""
"In December 2010, the community <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2010/12/06/kde-"
"announces-calligra-suite\">announces</a> the <a href=\"https://www.calligra."
"org/\">Calligra Suite</a>, a split from the KOffice suite. KOffice was "
"discontinued in 2011."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:702
msgctxt "id=\"box44-title\""
msgid "First Conf KDE India"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:709
msgctxt "id=\"box44\""
msgid ""
"In March 2011, the <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2010/12/28/confkdein-first-"
"kde-conference-india\">first conference</a> of the KDE and Qt community in "
"India took place in Bengaluru. Since then, the event has taken place "
"annually."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:715
msgctxt "id=\"box45-title\""
msgid "Desktop Summit 2011"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:722
msgctxt "id=\"box45\""
msgid ""
"In August 2011, <a href=\"https://desktopsummit.org/\">another joint "
"conference</a> of the KDE and Gnome communities took place in Berlin, "
"Germany. Nearly 800 contributors from all over the world came together to "
"share ideas and collaborate on various free software projects."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:728
msgctxt "id=\"box46-title\""
msgid "Plasma Active"
msgstr "Plasma Active"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:735
msgctxt "id=\"box46\""
msgid ""
"The community released the first version of its interface for mobile "
"devices, <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/plasma-active-one/"
"\">Plasma Active</a>. Later, it was superseded by Plasma Mobile."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:744
msgctxt "id=\"box47-title\""
msgid "First LaKademy"
msgstr "Primer LaKademy"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:751
msgctxt "id=\"box47\""
msgid ""
"In April 2012, the <a href=\"https://wiki.br.kde.org/LAkademy\">first "
"meeting</a> of the KDE contributors in Latin America, LaKademy, took place. "
"The event was held in Porto Alegre, Brazil. The <a href=\"https://br.kde.org/"
"lakademy-2014\">second edition</a> took place in 2014 in São Paulo, and "
"since then has been an annual event. So far, all editions were held in "
"Brazil, where the highest number of contributors from the Latin American "
"community is based."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:757
msgctxt "id=\"box48-title\""
msgid "KDE Manifesto"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:764
msgctxt "id=\"box48\""
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://manifesto.kde.org/index.html\">KDE Manifesto</a>, a "
"document that presents the benefits and obligations of a KDE project, was "
"released. It also introduces the core values that guide the community: Open "
"Governance, Free Software, Inclusivity, Innovation, Common Ownership, and "
"End-User Focus."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:770
msgctxt "id=\"box49-title\""
msgid "New Konqi"
msgstr "El Konqui nuevu"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:777
msgctxt "id=\"box49\""
msgid ""
"In December 2012, the community <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2012/12/08/"
"contest-create-konqi-krita\">launched a competition</a> to create a new "
"mascot using Krita. The competition winner was Tyson Tan, who created <a "
"href=\"http://tysontan.deviantart.com/art/Konqi-ver-2-494267237\">new looks "
"for the Konqi and Katie</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:786
msgctxt "id=\"box50-title\""
msgid "Release cycle change"
msgstr "Cambéu del ciclu de llanzamientos"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:793
msgctxt "id=\"box50\""
msgid ""
"In September 2013, the community <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2013/09/04/"
"kde-release-structure-evolves\">announced</a> changes in the release cycle "
"of its products. Each of them, Workspaces, Applications, and Platform, now "
"have separate releases. The change was already a reflection of the "
"restructuring of KDE technologies. This restructuring resulted in the next "
"generation of community products, which would be released the following year."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:802
msgctxt "id=\"box51-title\""
msgid "Frameworks 5"
msgstr "Frameworks 5"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:809
msgctxt "id=\"box51\""
msgid ""
"The first stable version of Frameworks 5 (KF5), the successor of KDE "
"Platform 4, <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/kde-frameworks-5.0."
"php\">was released</a>. This new generation of the KDE libraries based on Qt "
"5 has made the KDE development platform more modular and facilitated cross-"
"platform development."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:815
msgctxt "id=\"box52-title\""
msgid "Plasma 5"
msgstr "Plasma 5"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:822
msgctxt "id=\"box52\""
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/plasma5.0/\">Release</a> of the "
"first stable version of Plasma 5. This new generation of Plasma has a new "
"theme, Breeze. Changes include a migration to a new, fully hardware-"
"accelerated graphics stack centered around an OpenGL(ES) scenegraph. This "
"version of Plasma uses as base the Qt 5 and Frameworks 5."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:828
msgctxt "id=\"box53-title\""
msgid "GCompris joins the KDE"
msgstr "GCompris xúnese a KDE"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:835
msgctxt "id=\"box53\""
msgid ""
"In December 2014, the educational software suite <a href=\"https://dot.kde."
"org/2014/12/11/gcompris-joins-kde-incubator-and-launches-fundraiser"
"\">GCompris joins</a> the <a href=\"https://community.kde.org/Incubator"
"\">project incubator of KDE community</a>. Bruno Coudoin, who created the <a "
"href=\"http://gcompris.net/index-en.html\">project</a> in 2000, decided to "
"rewrite it in Qt Quick to facilitate its use on mobile platforms. It was "
"originally written in GTK+."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:841
msgctxt "id=\"box54-title\""
msgid "Plasma Mobile"
msgstr "Plasma Mobile"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:848
msgctxt "id=\"box54\""
msgid ""
"The community <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2015/07/25/plasma-mobile-free-"
"mobile-platform\">announced Plasma Mobile</a>, an interface for smartphones "
"that uses Qt, Frameworks 5 and Plasma Shell technologies."
msgstr ""
"La comunidá <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2015/07/25/plasma-mobile-free-"
"mobile-platform\">anunció Plasma Mobile</a>, una interfaz pa teléfonos "
"intelixentes qu'usa les teunoloxíes de Qt, Frameworks 5 y Plasma Shell."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:857
msgctxt "id=\"box55-title\""
msgid "Plasma on Wayland"
msgstr "Plasma en Wayland"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:864
msgctxt "id=\"box55\""
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2015/12/18/first-plasma-wayland-live-image"
"\">first live image</a> of Plasma running on Wayland was made available for "
"download. Since 2011, the community works in support of Wayland by KWin, the "
"Compositor of Plasma, and the Window Manager."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:870
msgctxt "id=\"box56-title\""
msgid "Plasma 5.5"
msgstr "Plasma 5.5"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:877
msgctxt "id=\"box56\""
msgid ""
"Version 5.5 is <a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/plasma-5.5.0.php"
"\">announced</a> with several new features: new icons added to the Breeze "
"theme, support for OpenGL ES in KWin, progress to support Wayland, a new "
"default font (Noto), a new design."
msgstr ""
"<a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/plasma-5.5.0.php\"> Anuncióse< /"
"a> la versión 5.5 con varies carauterístiques: iconos nuevos amestaos al "
"estilu Breeze, sofitu pa OpenGL ES en KWin, avances na compatibilidá con "
"Wayland, una fonte predeterminada nueva (Noto) y un diseñu nuevu."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:886
msgctxt "id=\"box57-title\""
msgid "KDE Neon"
msgstr "KDE Neon"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:893
msgctxt "id=\"box57\""
msgid ""
"The community <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2016/01/30/fosdem-announcing-kde-"
"neon\">announced</a> the inclusion of another project in its incubator, <a "
"href=\"https://neon.kde.org/\">KDE Neon</a>, based on Ubuntu. Developers, "
"testers, artists, translators and early adopters can get fresh code from git "
"as it is committed by the KDE community."
msgstr ""
"La comunidá <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2016/01/30/fosdem-announcing-kde-"
"neon\">anunció</a> la inclusión d'otru proyeutu na incubadora, <a"
" href=\"https "
"://neon.kde.org/\">KDE Neon</a>, basáu n'Ubuntu. Desendolcadores, probadores "
"artistes, traductores y usuarios esperimentales puen consiguir les versiones"
" más "
"nueves de los programes darréu que les forne direutamente la comunidá de KDE."

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:899
msgctxt "id=\"box58-title\""
msgid "Akademy 2016 part of QtCon"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:906
msgctxt "id=\"box58\""
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://akademy.kde.org/2016\">Akademy 2016</a> took place as a "
"part of <a href=\"http://qtcon.org/\">QtCon</a> in September 2016 in Berlin, "
"Germany. The event brought together the Qt, <a href=\"https://fsfe.org/"
"\">FSFE</a>, <a href=\"http://www.videolan.org/\">VideoLAN</a> and KDE "
"communities. It celebrated 20 years of KDE, 20 years of VLC, and 15 years of "
"FSFE."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:912
msgctxt "id=\"box59-title\""
msgid "Kirigami UI"
msgstr "IU de Kirigami"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:919
msgctxt "id=\"box59\""
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2016/03/30/kde-proudly-presents-kirigami-ui"
"\">Kirigami is released</a>, a set of QML components to develop applications "
"based on Qt for mobile or desktop devices."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:925
msgctxt "id=\"box60-title\""
msgid "KDE presents its Vision for the future"
msgstr "KDE presenta la so visión del futuru"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:929
msgctxt "id=\"box60\""
msgid ""
"In early 2016, as a result of a survey and open discussions among community "
"members, <a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2016/04/05/kde-presents-its-vision-"
"future\">KDE has published a document outlining its vision for the future</"
"a>. This vision represents the values that its members consider most "
"important: \"A world in which everyone has control over their digital life "
"and enjoys freedom and privacy.\" The idea in defining this vision was to "
"make clear what are the main motivations that drive the community."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:935
msgctxt "id=\"box61-title\""
msgid "KDE announced the Advisory Board"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:939
msgctxt "id=\"box61\""
msgid ""
"In order to formalize the cooperation among the community and the "
"organizations that have been its allies, <a href=\"https://dot.kde."
"org/2016/09/26/announcing-kde-advisory-board\">KDE e.V announced the "
"Advisory Board</a>. Through the Advisory Board, organizations can provide "
"feedback on community activities and decisions, to participate in regular "
"meetings with KDE e.V, and to attend to Akademy and community sprints."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:945
msgctxt "id=\"box62-title\""
msgid "KDE celebrated 20 years"
msgstr "KDE celebró los 20 años"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:950
msgctxt "id=\"box62\""
msgid ""
"On October 14, KDE celebrated its 20th birthday. The project that started as "
"a desktop environment for Unix systems, today is a\n"
"        community that incubates ideas and projects which go far beyond "
"desktop technologies. To celebrate its anniversary the community <a href="
"\"https://20years.kde.org/book/\">published a book</a> written by its "
"contributors. <a href=\"https://community.kde.org/Promo/Events/Parties/"
"KDE_20_Anniversary\">We also had parties</a> been held in eight countries."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:959
msgctxt "id=\"box63-title\""
msgid "KDE Slimbook is announced"
msgstr "Anúnciase'l KDE Slimbook"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:965
msgctxt "id=\"box63\""
msgid ""
"In partnership with a Spanish laptop retailer <a href=\"https://dot.kde."
"org/2017/01/26/kde-and-slimbook-release-laptop-kde-fans\">the community "
"announced the launch of the KDE Slimbook</a>, a ultrabook that comes with "
"the KDE Plasma and KDE Applications pre-installed. The laptop offers a pre-"
"installed version of KDE Neon and <a href=\"https://slimbook.es/en/store/"
"slimbook-kde\">can be purchased from the retailer's website</a>."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:971
msgctxt "id=\"box64-title\""
msgid "QtCon Brasil is announced"
msgstr "Anúnciase la QtCon de Brasil"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:976
msgctxt "id=\"box64\""
msgid ""
"Inspired by QtCon 2016, which took place in Berlin and brought together the "
"KDE, VLC, Qt and FSFE communities, <a href=\"https://br.qtcon.org/2017/"
"\">KDE community in Brazil hosted QtCon Brasil in 2017</a>. The event was "
"held in São Paulo and brought together Qt experts from Brazil and abroad in "
"two days of talks and one day of training."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:982
msgctxt "id=\"box65-title\""
msgid "KDE and Purism partnership"
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:987
msgctxt "id=\"box65\""
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://www.kde.org/announcements/kde-purism-librem5.php\">KDE and "
"Purism have partnered to adapt Plasma Mobile to the smartphone Librem 5</a>, "
"manufactured by the American company. Librem 5 is a phone focused on "
"preserving the privacy and security of user communication. The adaptation "
"project is underway and soon we will have the first phone in the world fully "
"controlled by the user and running Plasma Mobile."
msgstr ""

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:993
msgctxt "id=\"box66-title\""
msgid "KDE set goals"
msgstr "Eventos de KDE"

#: websites/timeline-kde-org/index.html:998
msgctxt "id=\"box66\""
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://dot.kde.org/2017/11/30/kdes-goals-2018-and-beyond\">KDE "
"sets its goals for the next four years</a>. As part of an effort undertaken "
"by its members since 2015, the community has defined three main objectives "
"for the coming years: to improve the usability and productivity of its "
"software, to ensure that its software helps to preserve the privacy of users "
"and to facilitate the contribution and integration of new collaborators."
msgstr ""
